    "hero": {
        "heading": "AG Grid vs TanStack Table",
        "subHeading": "Compare AG Grid vs TanStack Table, a data grid and a headless table library, on framework support, free and paid features, large datasets, pricing and licensing."
    },
    "shortAnswer": "AG Grid is a complete data grid that renders its own UI. TanStack Table is a headless library: it provides table state and logic, and you write the markup and CSS. Both have a free, MIT-licensed core. TanStack Table has no built-in virtualisation (it pairs with the separate TanStack Virtual package) and no cell editing in its core, and its built-in features do not include pivoting, CSV or Excel export, or charts. AG Grid Community includes virtualisation, cell editing and CSV export, and [AG Grid Enterprise](/license-pricing/), a paid perpetual licence, adds pivoting, Excel export and integrated charts.",
